WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.888
Now, who.

2
00:00:00.888 --> 00:00:05.712
The first connection asks an administrator
to consent to the tool's Microsoft

3
00:00:05.712 --> 00:00:10.537
Graph read permissions; later runs don't
ask again unless a new version adds one.

4
00:00:10.537 --> 00:00:12.174
The sources differ on who.

5
00:00:12.174 --> 00:00:14.262
Learn says a Global Administrator.

6
00:00:14.262 --> 00:00:19.202
The tool's guide for three point one point
oh says a Cloud Application Administrator

7
00:00:19.202 --> 00:00:23.437
or Application Administrator, and
that consent assigns no runtime role.

8
00:00:23.437 --> 00:00:28.463
Learn lists twenty-one permissions; the
source requests thirty-four, all read.

9
00:00:28.463 --> 00:00:30.750
The program follows the tool's guide.

10
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:34.737
The consent administrator consents
and doesn't run the assessment.

11
00:00:34.737 --> 00:00:39.250
The run account is a dedicated reader
whose roles are activated through pim

12
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:44.049
before each run; SharePoint Administrator
is the one write-capable role it needs.

13
00:00:44.049 --> 00:00:48.442
Consent lands on the shared Graph
PowerShell application by default,

14
00:00:48.442 --> 00:00:50.638
so the program uses a dedicated one.

15
00:00:50.638 --> 00:00:55.250
The guide's RACI names who is responsible
and accountable for each activity.
